    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "I tried with this : \r\n```javascript\r\npublic createURL(routeState: TRouteState): string {\r\n    const location = this.getLocation();\r\n    return new URL(\r\n      this._createURL({\r\n        qsModule: qs,\r\n        routeState,\r\n        location,\r\n      }),\r\n      location.href\r\n    ).href;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\nAnd it seems to work well, even with SSR provided their `getLocation` does return a URL.\r\n\r\nHowever I just realized that `URL` surprisingly [does not work in IE11](https://caniuse.com/?search=URL) 🤦",
